# Pending Work

## Observability — LGTM Stack (not started)

Add a new Terraform module at `deployments/local/cluster-admin/terraform/istio/observability/`
that wires Istio telemetry into a local LGTM stack.

### What to build
- Install `kube-prometheus-stack` (Prometheus + Grafana) via Helm
- Install `grafana/loki-stack` via Helm (access logs from Envoy)
- Install `grafana/tempo` via Helm (distributed traces)
- Patch Istio `meshConfig.extensionProviders` to point at Tempo/OTel collector
- Apply a `Telemetry` resource to enable Envoy access logging to Loki

### Why
- Tempo traces will show the two-leg request model visually:
  `IngressGateway span → IBM MQ pod span` confirming TLS termination + re-origination
- Loki access logs show per-request: protocol, hostname, path, status, upstream host, duration
- Metrics confirm request rates and error rates per service
- Note: TCP (port 443, IBM MQ wire) only gets metrics/access logs — no traces (protocol is opaque)

### Next step when resuming
Start with Tempo + Istio tracing config, test with an HTTPS console request,
verify the two spans appear in Grafana. Then add Loki for access logs.
